From: "lich.wang" <lich.wang@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] input: nt36532: scan for the pen by default and give it a resolution

The boot firmware update ends with "support pen = 0": the vendor's Android
user space turns pen scanning on later through /proc/support_pen. Without
that the pen reports nothing. When the DT marks the panel with
novatek,pen-support, start with pen scanning on; resume and the watchdog
recovery already restore ts->pen_state, and /proc/support_pen still
overrides it. A failed command is now logged instead of ignored.

libinput also drops a tablet without a resolution ("missing tablet
capabilities: resolution"). The pen reports 32000 x 20000 over the
273.5 x 171 mm panel: 117 units/mm on both axes (NVT_PEN_UNITS_PER_MM).

Tested on TB710FU (ArmadaOS desktop, no user-space setup): the pen
reports ABS_X/ABS_Y resolution 117, libinput lists NVTCapacitivePen as a
274x171mm tablet, and the pen taps and drags in KWin after boot.
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.c
@@ -2740,6 +2740,9 @@
 			     0, 0);
 	input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_Y, 0,
 			     PEN_MAX_HEIGHT, 0, 0);
+	/* libinput ignores a tablet without a resolution */
+	input_abs_set_res(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_X, NVT_PEN_UNITS_PER_MM);
+	input_abs_set_res(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_Y, NVT_PEN_UNITS_PER_MM);
 	input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_PRESSURE, 0,
 			     PEN_PRESSURE_MAX, 0, 0);
 	input_set_abs_params(ts->pen_input_dev, ABS_DISTANCE, 0,
@@ -3182,7 +3185,8 @@
 #if NVT_CUST_PROC_CMD
 	ts->edge_reject_state = 0;
 	ts->game_mode_state = 0;
-	ts->pen_state = 0;
+	/* scan for the pen by default when the DT says the panel has one */
+	ts->pen_state = ts->pen_support ? 1 : 0;
 #if NVT_DPR_SWITCH
 	ts->fw_pen_state = 0;
 #endif
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.h b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.h
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.h
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx.h
@@ -94,6 +94,8 @@
 #define NVT_PEN_NAME "NVTCapacitivePen"
 
 //---Touch info.---
+/* TB710FU: the pen reports 32000 x 20000 over the 273.5 x 171 mm panel */
+#define NVT_PEN_UNITS_PER_MM 117
 #ifdef BUILD_KIRBY_TOUCH
 #define NVT_SUPER_RESOLUTION_N 10
 #if NVT_SUPER_RESOLUTION_N
diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx_fw_update.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx_fw_update.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx_fw_update.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36532/nt36xxx_fw_update.c
@@ -923,7 +923,8 @@
 	mutex_unlock(&ts->lock);
 #if NVT_SUPPORT_PEN
 	if(ts->probe_state == 1){
-		nvt_support_pen_set(0);
+		if (nvt_support_pen_set(ts->pen_state))
+			NVT_ERR("set pen scanning to %d failed\n", ts->pen_state);
 		ts->probe_state = 0;
 	}
 #endif
-- 
